{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And YHWH descended in a pillar of cloud.</b> One needs to know why YHWH did not descend before the first summons, for it appears from the sequence of verses that He did not descend until after the summons. Moreover, what He said at the summons — ״צְאוּ שְׁלָשְׁתְּכֶם אֶל אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד״ — testifies that He had not yet descended, for otherwise there would have been no need to designate the place for them, since they would see the place where the cloud dwells. And according to the words of the commentators that we have written, that they were impure at the time of the summons, there is a sound reason for this: for YHWH did not wish to descend before the summons and sit and wait for them, as it were, until they come out, which is not consistent with His honor. Also, it would draw upon them, Heaven forbid, a punishment upon the summoned ones, and the Holy One, blessed is He, desires not to punish but to do good. And the reason YHWH descended and did not speak from His place in the order of the summons, was in order to publicize the matter when they would see that the cloud descended and stood at the entrance of the Tent — and this is a great publicity and proclamation, so that all Israel would know that YHWH took stern notice that they touched the faithful one of His house, and punished them for the matter."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:08.492650668Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}